{
    "background_story": "Paxton was a high-powered executive who had it all: a corner office, a six-figure salary, and a reputation as a business genius. But beneath the surface, he was struggling with an insatiable drive to succeed. Paxton's workaholism consumed him, forcing him to put in 12-hour days, 7 days a week. He would often sacrifice time with his loved ones, miss important milestones, and neglect his own well-being to stay ahead of the game. His colleagues admired his dedication, but his family and friends grew concerned about the toll it was taking on his mental and physical health. Despite the warnings, Paxton couldn't shake off the feeling that he was always one deal away from disaster. His workaholism had become an addiction, and he wasn't sure how to escape the vicious cycle.",
